WEBVTT

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.870
Hey, do you two have any plans for tonight?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.980
Huh? Tonight?

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:12.490
Yeah.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.400
Let's see...

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.290
I think I have club activities.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.490
It's probably fine though.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.610
Oh, by the way!

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.440
If we get together tonight, there's somewhere I want to go, ok?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.000
Ok! What about you, Eri?

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.750
Sorry, I have classes today...

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.770
But I should be free after ten.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.720
Cool!

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.890
We'll start after that, then.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.390
That settles it!

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.490
Tonight at ten, we'll meet at Mac Anu!

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.500
I'll make you the bait if you're late!

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.810
What's with that?

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.380
You're so childish.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.640
Damn...

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:28.230
Hey,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.480
what the-?!

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.720
Help me!

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.320
Nice!

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.920
Gah, this is becoming troublesome.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.730
What's that...?

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.120
Smoke bomb!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.810
Don't forget me!!!

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.090
That's our Tobias for you!

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.820
It's a good thing you're here!

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.950
There's no point in flattering me.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.860
Oh come now, don't be so shy.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.280
Thank you, too, Mary!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.870
Jeez, you're not even a beginner anymore...

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.810
How can you get lost in a straight tunnel?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.200
You know, even monkeys fall from trees sometimes.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.540
Nobody's perfect, right?

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.180
That goes for you, too.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.220
Just leave her.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.220
Not even death can cure idiocy of that magnitude.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.370
Sakuya-sensei is that kind of rare character.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.360
Hey, that hurts my pride!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.490
You have pride?

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.240
Wha-?! You're going to pay for that!!

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.990
Whoa, so that path led here!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.320
Yeah, into the lion's den.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.770
Lion's den? What makes you say that?

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:30.910
I'm getting bad vibes.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.630
But you can't win the jackpot without taking some risks.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.190
If we pass here, the contents of the treasure chest will change.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.710
And we can even avoid fighting the boss!

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.450
We won't fight? Some XP wouldn't-

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.660
Hey, what-?!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.070
I found something!

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.110
Sakuya!

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:49.620
What?

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.400
You're picking up trash again.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.790
See, that's why-

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.010
What's that?

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.060
Some guild plans to fight the boss.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.160
It's a dragon!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.260
The One Sin.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:20.690
The legendary beast of The World that can't be captured!

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:24.190
It's said to be pretty much invincible.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:31.410
The first ones to defeat it were given the name "Descendants of Fianna".

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.730
Is she drunk?

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.960
Seems so.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.810
It's invulnerable to physical attacks.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.110
Focus on elemental magic, as we planned!

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.030
Clerics, fall back to a safe distance!

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.030
They're planning to attack it head-on!

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.940
They look so pro!

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.600
Gotta take some screenshots!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.570
Just don't get lost!

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.600
It's gonna use Breath! Don't let it hit you!

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.910
Clerics, move in as soon as the cast is over!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.210
That Breath attack lasts way too long!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.100
What's going on?

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.550
What should I do...?

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.250
I stepped on something!

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.400
Can't you just stay still for a moment?

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.110
Is it over?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.530
Noise?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.670
Nothing on the sensors.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.620
Just an Event?

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.560
No way!

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.670
Tobi-chan!

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.860
Breath incoming! Hurry!

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.280
The boss has an area of effect trap?

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:30.960
Screw this.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.370
Look, there!

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.370
Tobias, the information dealer?

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.980
It won't follow us this far.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:01.850
No way...!

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.660
This boss is way too strong!

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.000
Mary!

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.670
We're all dead if it casts a fire spell here!

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:28.600
We are, aren't we?

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.450
Oi, wait!

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:42.990
Are you an idiot, Sakuya?!

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.980
I distracted it so you could get away! So why did you jump in too?!

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.770
But if we left,

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.200
how would you get away?

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:52.740
Come, hurry!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.880
We're running!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.090
Hurry!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.470
Hooray! I thought for sure we were dead!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.720
Jeez, and whose fault would that have been?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.260
And we didn't even get the rare item.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.430
We almost died there for nothing.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.060
Not true.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:30.660
In this game, everything that happened just now was real.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:35.440
To me, memories like this are worth more than anything.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.710
Tobias...

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.180
Where did you get that rare mantle?

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.840
Huh, what?

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.330
Nothing can escape the attention of the great Tobias!

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.330
To think that I was worried...

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.550
Today was a lot of fun.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.350
Yep!

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.350
Loads of fun.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.220
The World!

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.620
Asumi! Asumi!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.450
Wake up already!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.500
I'm on it...

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.660
Eri-chan is already here!

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:31.500
No way!

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.640
Why the hell is my alarm clock off?!

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:47.900
If you have some time on the way home, could you buy tissues?

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.660
Gah, why me?

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:54.960
Huh? I told you not to order me around!

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.800
I'm off!

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.610
Sorry! Let's go!

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.530
Why do you have to oversleep every morning?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:06.410
Rather, how can you wake up perfectly even when we go to sleep at the same time?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.820
My alarm clock-

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.230
That didn't work.

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:09.920
Idiot!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.630
Wait!

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.180
We've gotta take this bus!

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.140
Stop!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.060
We've got to get on!

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.370
Great, it stopped!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.520
Hurry, hurry!

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.240
Thank god, we made it...

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.590
You're wasting both your sweat, and your youth.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.240
And not in small amounts, either.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.070
Damn.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.800
Wait, what's with those clothes? Are you nuts?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.210
None of your business.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.800
As you can see, I prefer practicality.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.460
At least in the real world.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.420
Why are you wearing that?

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.250
In the game, you prefer aesthetics!

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:06.190
Why are you such a disappointment in reality?

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.840
Get over it.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:10.810
Next, we'll talk about the microchip

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.060
that all of you have in your bodies.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.390
That which we call an "implant".

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:18.370
Why is such a device necessary?

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.740
Why did humankind choose to advance cybernetic technology?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.740
The price of raw materials is still falling.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.390
Why did humankind choose to advance cybernetic technology?

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:27.880
Could it have something to do with the new item drop in next month's mission?

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:30.490
I had better sell everything while I still can.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:35.000
Encoding methods have made significant advances.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:41.140
It became necessary to implement a universal verification method.

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:44.400
This applies to personal authentication as well.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.020
Where passwords and authentication keys were used in the past...

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.020
A bounty of 300000 GP?!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:56.400
Malicious interference with and interruption of a mission.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.030
The death of sixteen guild members.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.790
Contact the Yata no Kagami guild.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.410
I'm dead.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:10.130
Congratulations! Now you're famous too!

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.730
That's not funny!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.550
We were all there!

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:18.300
How will I be able to live in The World from now on?

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.840
Asumi-san, wouldn't this be a good opportunity to take a break from the game?

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.050
The exams are nearing as well...

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:28.280
Are you conspiring with my mother, Eri?

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.740
I'm fine, 'cause I just cram everything in one night.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.230
Oh, then I'll do that too!

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:35.960
It'll be all right if I remember everything when exams arrive!

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.930
No, it won't be!

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:40.940
Your grades are nowhere as good as Iori's!

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:44.090
We'll be graduating next year!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:46.220
You're so mean today.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:50.130
I won't be playing until the exams are over, either.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.100
We need to start thinking about what we're doing next year...

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:57.610
I guess we'll be playing The World together then, too!

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:58.960
Asumi!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.980
But you know,

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:07.550
a year ago, I thought "I'll just go to school and graduate."

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:14.680
But now that I'm playing The World, home and school aren't the only things in my life. It feels good.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.540
There's a world outside school...

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:22.420
Well, there are troubles there too, like that guild...

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.330
But things like that are rare...

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:30.370
And I became friends with Iori too, so I don't want to stop.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.510
It's also fun that I can play with Eri again, like we used to.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:36.870
But I'm causing so much trouble,

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.350
I'm afraid you'll get really mad at me sometime.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.500
I want to go to the same university as Eri, you know.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.830
I really was thinking about my future!

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.820
Really?!

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:52.210
If you think about it, it's a really simple solution.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.890
Right then!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.560
Tonight, let's meet at our usual place!

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.400
And what's the solution then?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.200
You'll see if you show up!

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.540
Did she really think about it?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:11.330
What if she said, "Let's study in The World!"?

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:33.810
Dear players! This area will soon be undergoing server maint-

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.010
Stop!

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:48.580
You're mistaking me for someone else!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.290
All of this hassle over a single bounty...

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:04.160
Mary and Tobias said they're not coming either...

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:04.800
This sucks.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.800
And here I was, hoping we could study in The World...

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.300
Would they forgive me if I apologized?

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:15.560
Wha-?!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.450
A bite?! Yeah!

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.920
And it's a big one, a big one!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.760
Did you find her?

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:30.820
Nope.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.980
Did she log out?

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.680
We have the gate covered.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.020
She must be somewhere that we haven't searched yet. Go!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.830
What's this?

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:46.470
The World feels a bit too real lately, doesn't it?

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.510
It's so vivid.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.500
There you go.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.150
Thanks.

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:56.210
You're welcome.

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:59.400
I'm As- i mean, Sakuya. Nice to meet you.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:01.820
I'm Hermit.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:02.920
Hermit?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.190
From tarot?

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.290
Kinda.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.310
You have a bounty on your head, right?

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.210
Yeah...

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.610
You're not from that guild, are you?!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.570
No.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.480
But I was there too, yesterday.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:22.580
Did you pick up anything strange there?

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.600
Anything strange...?

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:30.210
I pick up pretty much everything I find...

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.220
Is it a rare item?

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.530
Eh, it doesn't matter if you don't know.

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.720
One more thing.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.720
The two that were with you in that arena...

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:42.610
are they coming today?

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.640
Ah, Tobias and Mary?

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:48.220
They're not coming today, but I'll introduce you next time!

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.170
They're my friends. We usually play together.

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.390
...Friends?

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:54.240
There she is!

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.180
Who did this?!

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.240
Who posted this in the name of the guild?!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:06.000
I don't recall authorizing such an abuse of power!

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:09.250
It was the freelancers... they posted it on their own.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:14.190
Then request removal before the situation gets even worse!

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.050
Umm...

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:17.260
What is it?!

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:20.640
Umm... my deepest apologies,

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.980
but they've already caught...

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:28.740
It hurts... not.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.010
Give up.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:33.030
Those bags are hacked. You can't escape.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:37.790
If you just log out, your account will be wiped clean.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:40.630
If you want to live, call the two that were with you yesterday.

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:44.540
I won't! I told you, I was the one that triggered the trap!

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:48.960
Also, I only just became friends with Hermit-san!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.630
Please don't get him involved!

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:55.890
Are you looking down on us?

00:17:55.890 --> 00:18:00.450
Did you think that preparing for that mission was an easy task?

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:04.870
Did you think we'd just let you go if you apologized?

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:07.060
I was hoping...

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:14.820
You're terrible.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.320
Jesus. Don't make us look bad.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.820
You started this.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:25.130
Did you think we'd just let the other two escape if we caught you?

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:31.520
Well, it doesn't matter. It seems like you value your old friends more than your new ones.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:32.340
You coward!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.390
I told you not to bring him into this!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.550
Damn! She's fighting back!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.140
Sakuya!

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.770
Hey, wait a second!

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:55.230
We can't see anything!

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:58.900
Iyoten, are you okay?

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.110
Look for her!

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:01.920
Kill her, if you have to!

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:02.780
Huh? How? How did you do that?

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.430
A backdoor.

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.080
There she is!

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:09.660
Sakuya, we're here to save you!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.670
Stop!

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:14.290
But it seems like you're fine!

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.710
Tobias!

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:17.760
Why are you here?

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.220
You said you weren't logging on today!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.100
I guess I just saw the bat signal over the city.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:29.230
There were messages on the BBS that the girl with the bounty is being chased across town.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.230
Come on, at least act your age at times like this!

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:34.480
Iyote?

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:38.920
The freelancer that joined us for The One Sin?

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:43.140
Yeah. When I looked into it, I learned that he had been involved in similar cases in the past.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:48.240
So I looked up his location data and tracked him here.

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:50.580
You're so good at gathering intel!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.900
Like taking candy from a baby.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:53.250
Sorry, Hermit-san.

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:56.550
We've gotten you involved in our troubles.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.840
D-Don't worry about it...

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.260
Hermit,

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.290
thanks for earlier!

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:02.970
Here!

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.130
For saving me!

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:10.320
Kinda... Just don't be disappointed if it turns out to be junk.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.740
There! They're over there!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.120
They're here already!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.750
I guess stunning wasn't enough for them.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.960
Those idiots! Come!

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.690
Ouch!

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:46.200
Sorry!

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:52.430
A Smoke Bomb?

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:05.650
Get in front of them!

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.530
They're so persistent!

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:11.540
You there!

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:14.540
We have to talk! Come down here!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.030
Damn!

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:17.210
Ignore them!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.170
Looks like their boss showed up!

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.040
Ignore them!

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:21.690
You're not getting away!

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.020
Damn!

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:37.810
This is bad...

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:39.310
Smith!

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:40.690
Asta!

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.190
Throw them down!

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:52.950
Sakuya!

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.190
Hermit!

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.720
I'll PK you first.

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:12.010
Don't!

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:13.020
Stop!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.220
Hermit!

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:24.770
What's this?!

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:35.160
Where are we?

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:37.780
It's not an implemented field.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:39.190
The boss!

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:42.480
Yeah. Where are the others?

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:52.980
What's that? People?

00:22:57.750 --> 00:22:58.610
What?!

00:22:58.610 --> 00:22:59.640
Sophia...

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:01.100
Sakuya!

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:03.700
Sakuya! Log out right now!

00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:04.610
This place is dangerous!

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:07.000
Mary! Tobias!

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.110
Where's Hermit?

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.670
No idea!

00:23:09.670 --> 00:23:11.700
If he got killed, he'll be back in town!

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:12.550
But-

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.700
Mary, don't bother!

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:19.570
Smith!

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:26.750
What happened?

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:28.130
I was unprepared.

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:31.760
This whole area is a pariah folder!

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.110
What do you mean?

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:35.150
Ouch!

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:40.130
Mary!

00:23:41.490 --> 00:23:42.810
This hurts!

00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:49.380
What's that?

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:51.360
Dunno. We'll talk about it later!

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:53.710
Log out right now!

00:23:55.120 --> 00:23:56.310
I'll email you later.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:58.380
Sakuya!

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:03.280
Mary!

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:11.010
What's going on?!

00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:11.870
Eri!

00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:42.040
With a feverish heat
Ukareta netsu no naka ni

00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:47.270
Sleeping more in the day than ever before
Ikudo to sugiru hi no nemuri

00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:57.210
When I woke up what did I see to make my heart dance?
Mezameta toki ni mune wa nani wo mite odoru no ka

00:24:57.210 --> 00:25:06.050
Where did I promise to return to?
Doko he modoru to yakusoku shita no?

00:25:06.050 --> 00:25:18.840
We can't return to the ever-repeating old memories
Kurikaeshita tooi kioku ni wa kaerenai

00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:26.510
Please, that moment of happiness
Negai yo, hitotoki no yorokobi ni

00:25:26.510 --> 00:25:29.340
Should last forever
Towa wo egaite

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:38.750
If those sunk in sorrow cried that there's no help,
Sukui wa nai to shizumi yuku mono ga naita nara

00:25:38.750 --> 00:25:50.640
Remember the warmth that wasn't faked
Mayakasi ja nai nukumori wo omoidashite

00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:01.370
Coma.

00:26:01.370 --> 00:26:02.490
Sleepers.

00:26:02.490 --> 00:26:03.270
Past.

00:26:03.270 --> 00:26:04.330
Present.

00:26:04.330 --> 00:26:05.370
Legend.

00:26:05.370 --> 00:26:06.390
Truth.

00:26:06.390 --> 00:26:07.790
Personal data.

00:26:07.790 --> 00:26:08.910
Ghost.

00:26:08.910 --> 00:26:10.490
Password crack.

00:26:10.490 --> 00:26:12.080
Implant chip.

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:13.030
Investigation.

00:26:13.030 --> 00:26:14.200
Concealment.

00:26:14.200 --> 00:26:15.380
Destruction.

00:26:15.380 --> 00:26:18.550
.hack//Quantum. Please watch the next one too.
